From fb5a372cb867a1d95b59283def91ac2b77689f03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viren070 <viren070@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:45:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ass_render: render events on helper threads

ass_set_threads() sets how many threads render a frame's events, by
default one per processor up to 8. The calling thread renders too, and
wakes helpers only for frames predicted to take more than 16 ms, as
few as are predicted to bring the frame under that: each event is
expected to cost what it did last frame, and a new one what new events
of its layer and style have lately. Costly events go first. Frames whose
threads keep waiting for each other's cache items use fewer.
